`conduct also punishable under another written law` MEANS `Proposed Act` WITH
    `actor` IS `adult Alice`
    `place of the act` IS `wholly in Singapore`
    `place of any other relevant act` IS `wholly in Singapore`
    `intends to make a gain or cause a loss or harm` IS FALSE
    `intends to cause exposure to a risk of loss` IS FALSE
    `that gain loss or harm occurs in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the person is liable by law to be tried in Singapore for an offence committed beyond Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the act would constitute an offence under Chapter 6 or Chapter 6B if committed in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is or may be punishable under another written law in force` IS TRUE
    `exception facts` IS `blank exception facts`
    `private defence facts` IS `blank private defence`
    `fault` IS `blank fault`
    `deception` IS `no deception`
    `personal information dealing` IS `blank personal information`
    `services obtained` IS `blank services`
    `fraud conduct` IS `blank fraud`
    `property taking` IS `blank property taking`
    `trust` IS `blank trust`
    `document making` IS `blank document making`
    `speech` IS `blank speech`
    `abetment` IS `blank abetment`
    `conspiracy` IS `blank conspiracy`
    `attempt` IS `blank attempt`
    `homicide` IS `blank homicide`
    `bodily harm` IS `blank bodily harm`
    `personal liberty` IS `blank personal liberty`
    `unborn and infants` IS `blank unborn and infants`
    `kidnapping` IS `blank kidnapping`

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 4A, the right of private defence`

-- s 96 with ss 97(a), 101 and 103: the right, exercised below the death ceiling.
#ASSERT `a private defence justification is made out` `defending the body without killing`
-- s 103: the same facts plus a killing fall outside the right.
#ASSERT NOT (`a private defence justification is made out` `killing the assailant with no section 102 description`)
-- s 102(a): the killing is within the right once death was reasonably apprehended.
#ASSERT `a private defence justification is made out` `killing the assailant under section 102(a)`
-- s 98(2): no right at all where a public authority could have been resorted to.
#ASSERT NOT (`a private defence justification is made out` `defending the body with recourse to a public authority available`)
-- s 98(1): no right where more harm than necessary is inflicted.
#ASSERT NOT (`a private defence justification is made out` `defending the body with more harm than necessary`)
-- s 99: the right survives the assailant's incapacity, with no separate offence element.
#ASSERT `a private defence justification is made out` `defending against an assailant of unsound mind`
-- s 106A(1): the bar bites against a public servant known to be one.
#ASSERT NOT (`a private defence justification is made out` `defending against a public servant acting in good faith`)
-- s 106A(1): and does not bite where death or grievous hurt is reasonably apprehended.
#ASSERT `a private defence justification is made out` `defending against a public servant who threatens death`
-- s 104(2): the property right ends when the thief has effected his retreat.
#ASSERT NOT (`a private defence justification is made out` `defending property against a thief who has got away`)
#ASSERT `a private defence justification is made out` `defending property against a thief still at it`
-- s 105(1)(a) and s 106: death is within the right against robbery, not against theft.
#ASSERT `a private defence justification is made out` `killing a robber`
#ASSERT NOT (`a private defence justification is made out` `killing a thief`)

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 5, sections 111, 113 and 114`

-- s 111 with its proviso, on Illustration (a).
#ASSERT `the abettor is liable under section 111 for the different act done` `instigation where a different act was done`
-- Illustration (b): a distinct act is not a probable consequence, so s 111 does not reach it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the abettor is liable under section 111 for the different act done` `instigation where a distinct act was done`)
-- s 113 turns on the knowledge proviso, and fails without it.
#ASSERT `the abettor is liable under section 113 for the different effect caused` `instigation causing an effect the abettor knew was likely`
#ASSERT NOT (`the abettor is liable under section 113 for the different effect caused` `instigation causing an unforeseen effect`)
-- s 114: presence converts abetment into principal liability.
#ASSERT `the abettor is deemed to have committed the act or offence under section 114` `abettor present at the commission`
-- and does not fire on an abettor who was absent.
#ASSERT NOT (`the abettor is deemed to have committed the act or offence under section 114` `instigation where a different act was done`)

§§ `Assertions -- the private defence wiring, and Chapter 1 sections 3, 4A and 5`

-- The point of the rewiring: a taking that satisfies s 378 in every element is not
-- theft when it is done in the exercise of the right of private defence (s 6).
#ASSERT `constitutes theft` (`disarming an assailant`'s `property taking`) (`disarming an assailant`'s `fault`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the proposed act constitutes theft` `disarming an assailant`)
#ASSERT `the proposed act constitutes theft` `taking a knife with no defence`
#ASSERT NOT (`any screened offence is indicated` `disarming an assailant`)
#ASSERT `any screened offence is indicated` `taking a knife with no defence`
-- s 6 reports the Chapter 4A route as well as the Chapter 4 one.
#ASSERT `the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` `disarming an assailant`
#ASSERT NOT (`a general exception applies` `disarming an assailant`)
-- s 3, s 4A: both bring a foreign act within the territorial screen.
#ASSERT `the act is dealt with under this Code as if committed within Singapore` `act abroad by a person triable in Singapore`
#ASSERT `Singapore has territorial reach over the proposed act` `act abroad by a person triable in Singapore`
#ASSERT `the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A` `genocide abroad by a citizen`
#ASSERT `Singapore has territorial reach over the proposed act` `genocide abroad by a citizen`
-- and neither fires on an act wholly within Singapore with neither fact asserted.
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is dealt with under this Code as if committed within Singapore` `innocent act in Singapore`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the act is deemed committed in Singapore under section 4A` `innocent act in Singapore`)
-- s 5: the saving is reported, and no encoded offence is indicated on the same facts.
#ASSERT `another written law is unaffected and may still apply` `conduct also punishable under another written law`
#ASSERT NOT (`any screened offence is indicated` `conduct also punishable under another written law`)

#EVAL `the offence screen of` `disarming an assailant`

§§ `Homicide fixtures -- Chapter 16, sections 299 to 311`

-- s 299 with s 300(a): death caused with the intention of causing death, and no Exception.
`a plain intentional killing` MEANS Homicide WITH
    `causes death by doing an act` IS TRUE
    `with the intention of causing death` IS TRUE
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as is likely to cause death` IS FALSE
    `with the knowledge that he is likely by such act to cause death` IS FALSE
    `the deceased was labouring under a disorder disease or bodily infirmity and the bodily injury accelerated the death` IS FALSE
    `the death might have been prevented by resorting to proper remedies and skilful treatment` IS FALSE
    `the death caused is that of a child in the mother womb` IS FALSE
    `any part of the child had been brought forth though the child may not have breathed or been completely born` IS FALSE
    `the act by which the death is caused is done with the intention of causing death` IS TRUE
    `with the intention of causing such bodily injury as the offender knows to be likely to cause the death of the person to whom the harm is caused` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of causing bodily injury to any person and the bodily injury intended to be inflicted is sufficient in the ordinary course of nature to cause death` IS FALSE
    `knows that the act is so imminently dangerous that it must in all probability cause death or such bodily injury as is likely to cause death and commits it without any excuse for incurring the risk` IS FALSE
    `whilst deprived of the power of self-control by grave and sudden provocation causes the death of the person who gave the provocation or of any other person by mistake or accident` IS FALSE
    `an ordinary person of the same gender and age sharing such characteristics as would affect the gravity of the provocation and placed in the same situation would be deprived of self-control by it` IS FALSE
    `the provocation was sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for killing or doing harm to any person` IS FALSE
    `the offender knew or had reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of the powers of such public servant` IS FALSE
    `the provocation was given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence` IS FALSE
    `in the exercise of the right of private defence of person or property exceeds the power given by law and causes the death of the person against whom the right is exercised` IS FALSE
    `without premeditation as defined in the Explanation to Exception 2` IS FALSE
    `without any intention of doing more harm than is necessary for the purpose of such defence` IS FALSE
    `being a public servant or aiding a public servant acting for the advancement of public justice exceeds the powers given to him by law` IS FALSE
    `causes death by doing an act which he in good faith believes to be lawful and necessary for the due discharge of his duty as such public servant` IS FALSE
    `without ill will towards the person whose death is caused` IS FALSE
    `committed without premeditation in a sudden fight in the heat of passion upon a sudden quarrel` IS FALSE
    `without the offender having taken undue advantage or acted in a cruel or unusual manner` IS FALSE
    `the offender knew or had reason to believe that the person whose death was caused was acting in obedience to the law or was a public servant acting in the lawful exercise of the powers of such public servant` IS FALSE
    `the person whose death is caused being above 18 years of age suffers death or takes the risk of death with his own consent` IS FALSE
    `the offender being a woman voluntarily causes the death of her child being a child below 12 months of age` IS FALSE
    `at the time of the offence the balance of her mind was disturbed by reason of her not having fully recovered from the effect of giving birth to the child or by reason of the effect of lactation consequent upon the birth` IS FALSE
    `at the time of the acts or omissions causing the death the offender was suffering from such abnormality of mind as substantially impaired his capacity to know the nature of those acts or omissions` IS FALSE
    `such abnormality of mind substantially impaired his capacity to know whether those acts or omissions are wrong` IS FALSE
    `such abnormality of mind substantially impaired his power to control his acts or omissions` IS FALSE
    `there was a substantial impairment of his capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong by the ordinary standards of reasonable and honest persons` IS FALSE
    `there was a substantial impairment of his capacity to know that the acts or omissions are wrong as contrary to law` IS FALSE
    `by doing anything which he intends or knows to be likely to cause death causes the death of a person whose death he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause` IS FALSE
    `causes the death of any person by doing a rash or negligent act not amounting to culpable homicide` IS FALSE
    `the victim is a child below 14 years of age a domestic worker or a vulnerable person` IS FALSE
    `the accused is a relevant person in relation to the victim within section 304B(2)` IS FALSE
    `causes the death of the victim by a course of conduct consisting of voluntarily causing hurt or knowingly causing neglect or both` IS FALSE
    `that course of conduct occurred on 2 or more occasions` IS FALSE
    `that course of conduct occurred on a single occasion and was protracted` IS FALSE
    `the victim dies as a result of the unlawful act of a person who was a member of the same household as the victim and had frequent contact with the victim` IS FALSE
    `the accused was a member of the same household as the victim and had frequent contact with the victim at the time of that act` IS FALSE
    `at that time there was a significant risk of grievous hurt being caused to the victim by the unlawful act of such a person` IS FALSE
    `the accused was the person whose act caused the victim death` IS FALSE
    `the accused was or ought to have been aware of that significant risk` IS FALSE
    `the accused failed to take such steps as could reasonably have been expected to protect the victim from that significant risk` IS FALSE
    `the unlawful act occurred in circumstances of the kind that the accused foresaw or ought to have foreseen` IS FALSE
    `the accused could not have been expected in the accused circumstances to take any such step` IS FALSE
    `abets the commission of the suicide or attempted suicide` IS FALSE
    `that person commits suicide` IS FALSE
    `that person attempts suicide` IS FALSE
    `the person who committed or attempted suicide is a minor below 18 years of age or a person who lacks capacity to understand the consequences of attempting or committing suicide` IS FALSE
    `knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person was such a minor or person who lacks capacity` IS FALSE
    `hurt is caused to any person in the course of the attempted suicide` IS FALSE
    `does any act with the intention of causing death` IS FALSE
    `under such circumstances that if he by that act caused death he would be guilty of murder` IS FALSE
    `under such circumstances that if he by that act caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide not amounting to murder` IS FALSE
    `hurt is caused to any person by such act` IS FALSE
    `is or acts as a member of a group` IS FALSE
    `knowing that the common object of the members of the group is to commit an offence under this Code or any written law` IS FALSE
    `knowing that death or grievous hurt is likely to be caused in furtherance of the group common object` IS FALSE
    `knowing that a deadly weapon or anything which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death is to be used against another person in furtherance of that common object` IS FALSE
    `the death of a person was caused in furtherance of the group common object` IS FALSE
    `intentionally or knowingly conceals desecrates or disposes of a human corpse` IS FALSE
    `by such act impedes or prevents the discovery or identification of a human corpse` IS FALSE
    `by such act impedes or prevents the detection investigation or prosecution of an offence under this Code or any other written law` IS FALSE
    `the woman by an intentional act or omission causes the death of her child being a child below 12 months of age` IS FALSE

