§§ `Restraint, force and assault fixtures -- Chapter 16, sections 339 to 358`

-- s 339 with its Illustration: obstructing a path Z has a right to pass along, without believing in good faith in a right to stop it.
`blocking a path` MEANS `Personal Liberty` WITH
    `voluntarily obstructs any person so as to prevent that person from proceeding in any direction in which that person has a right to proceed` IS TRUE
    `the obstruction is of a private way over land or water which the accused in good faith believes himself to have a lawful right to obstruct` IS FALSE
    `the restraint prevents that person from proceeding beyond certain circumscribing limits` IS FALSE
    `keeps the person in wrongful confinement knowing that a writ for the liberation of that person has been duly issued` IS FALSE
    `confines in such a manner as to indicate an intention that the confinement or the place of it may not be known to or discovered by any person interested in the person confined or any public servant` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined or from any person interested in him any property or valuable security` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined or any person interested in him to do anything illegal or to give any information which may facilitate the commission of an offence` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of extorting from the person confined or from any person interested in him any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct` IS FALSE
    `for the purpose of constraining the person confined or any person interested in him to restore or to cause the restoration of any property or valuable security or to satisfy any claim or demand or to give information which may lead to such restoration` IS FALSE
    `causes motion change of motion or cessation of motion to that other` IS FALSE
    `causes to any substance such motion change of motion or cessation of motion as brings that substance into contact with any part of that other body or with anything that other is wearing or carrying or with anything so situated that such contact affects that other sense of feeling` IS FALSE
    `by his own bodily power` IS FALSE
    `by disposing any substance in such a manner that the motion or change or cessation of motion takes place without any further act on his part or on the part of any other person` IS FALSE
    `by inducing any animal to move to change its motion or to cease to move` IS FALSE
    `intentionally uses force to any person` IS FALSE
    `without that person consent` IS FALSE
    `in order to cause the committing of any offence` IS FALSE
    `intending by the use of such force illegally to cause injury fear or annoyance to the person to whom the force is used` IS FALSE
    `knowing it to be likely that by the use of such force he will illegally cause injury fear or annoyance to that person` IS FALSE
    `makes any gesture or any preparation` IS FALSE
    `intending or knowing it to be likely that such gesture or preparation will cause any person present to apprehend that he is about to use criminal force to that person` IS FALSE
    `the case rests on words alone unaccompanied by any gesture or preparation` IS FALSE
    `on grave and sudden provocation given by that person` IS FALSE
    `the provocation was sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for the offence` IS FALSE
    `the offender knows or has reason to believe that the provocation is given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of the powers of such public servant` IS FALSE
    `the provocation is given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence` IS FALSE
    `the person assaulted is a public servant in the execution of his duty as such public servant` IS FALSE
    `with intent to prevent or deter that person from discharging his duty as such public servant` IS FALSE
    `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant` IS FALSE
    `intending to outrage or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby outrage the modesty of that person` IS FALSE
    `the person is below 14 years of age` IS FALSE
    `in order to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence under section 354` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily causes or attempts to cause to that person death or hurt or wrongful restraint or fear of instant death instant hurt or instant wrongful restraint` IS FALSE
    `the offence is committed in a lift in any building` IS FALSE
    `intending thereby to dishonour that person` IS FALSE
    `in committing or attempting to commit theft of any property which that person is then wearing or carrying` IS FALSE
    `in attempting wrongfully to confine that person` IS FALSE

