§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, offences affecting life`

-- s 299 with s 300(a), no Exception: murder.
#ASSERT `constitutes culpable homicide` `a plain intentional killing`
#ASSERT `constitutes murder` `a plain intentional killing`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes culpable homicide not amounting to murder` `a plain intentional killing`)
-- Exception 1 returns the same facts to culpable homicide.
#ASSERT `Exception 1 applies` `a killing on grave and sudden provocation`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes murder` `a killing on grave and sudden provocation`)
#ASSERT `constitutes culpable homicide not amounting to murder` `a killing on grave and sudden provocation`
-- Illustration (c) to Exception 1: proviso (b) defeats it, so this is murder again.
#ASSERT NOT (`Exception 1 applies` `a killing on provocation given by a lawful arrest`)
#ASSERT `constitutes murder` `a killing on provocation given by a lawful arrest`
-- Exceptions 2 and 5.
#ASSERT `Exception 2 applies` `a killing that exceeds private defence`
#ASSERT `constitutes culpable homicide not amounting to murder` `a killing that exceeds private defence`
#ASSERT `Exception 5 applies` `a suicide pact death by consent`
#ASSERT `constitutes culpable homicide not amounting to murder` `a suicide pact death by consent`
-- Explanation 3 to s 299: the child in the womb, and the child partly brought forth.
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes culpable homicide` `a death in the womb`)
#ASSERT `constitutes culpable homicide` `a death of a child partly brought forth`
-- s 304A is defined as not amounting to culpable homicide, and does not overlap it.
#ASSERT `constitutes causing death by a rash or negligent act` `a fatal traffic accident`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes culpable homicide` `a fatal traffic accident`)
-- s 307 is complete without a death.
#ASSERT `constitutes attempt to murder` `an attempt to murder that fails`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes murder` `an attempt to murder that fails`)

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, hurt`

#ASSERT `hurt is caused` `a punch causing pain`
#ASSERT `hurt is voluntarily caused` `a punch causing pain`
#ASSERT NOT (`grievous hurt is caused` `a punch causing pain`)
-- s 322 and its Explanation: the kind intended and the kind caused need not match.
#ASSERT `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` `a blow intended to disfigure that breaks a bone`
-- s 323A: grievous hurt caused, but not intended, so not s 322.
#ASSERT `hurt is voluntarily caused which causes grievous hurt` `a punch that unexpectedly paralyses`
#ASSERT NOT (`grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` `a punch that unexpectedly paralyses`)
-- ss 324, 330 and 328.
#ASSERT `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt by dangerous weapons or means` `a stabbing`
#ASSERT `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt to extort a confession` `torture to extract a confession`
#ASSERT `constitutes causing hurt by poison with intent to commit an offence` `poison administered to facilitate an offence`
-- s 328 needs no hurt in fact; the fixture asserts none.
#ASSERT NOT (`hurt is caused` `poison administered to facilitate an offence`)
-- ss 336 and 337: the rash act alone, and the rash act causing hurt.
#ASSERT `constitutes an act endangering life or personal safety` `driving that endangers others`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes causing hurt by an act endangering life` `driving that endangers others`)
#ASSERT `constitutes causing hurt by an act endangering life` `driving that endangers others and injures one`

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, restraint, force and assault`

#ASSERT `the person is wrongfully restrained` `blocking a path`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is wrongfully confined` `blocking a path`)
-- The Exception written into s 339 itself.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is wrongfully restrained` `blocking a private way in good faith`)
-- s 340: confinement is restraint within circumscribing limits.
#ASSERT `the person is wrongfully confined` `locking a person in a room`
#ASSERT `the person is wrongfully restrained` `locking a person in a room`
-- ss 349 and 350.
#ASSERT `force is used to another` `pushing someone in the street`
#ASSERT `criminal force is used` `pushing someone in the street`
-- s 351: an assault needs no force, and words alone are not an assault.
#ASSERT `an assault is committed` `shaking a fist`
#ASSERT NOT (`force is used to another` `shaking a fist`)
#ASSERT NOT (`an assault is committed` `a threat in words alone`)
-- ss 352 and 358, and the Explanation that disqualifies a sought provocation.
#ASSERT `constitutes assault or criminal force on provocation` `a shove on grave and sudden provocation`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes assault or criminal force otherwise than on provocation` `a shove on grave and sudden provocation`)
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes assault or criminal force on provocation` `a shove on provocation sought as an excuse`)
#ASSERT `constitutes assault or criminal force otherwise than on provocation` `a shove on provocation sought as an excuse`

§§ `Unborn children and infants fixtures -- Chapter 16, sections 312 to 318`

-- ss 312 and 313: a miscarriage voluntarily caused, outside the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974, without the woman's consent.
`a miscarriage caused without consent` MEANS `Unborn And Infants` WITH
    `the act is within the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry` IS TRUE
    `the woman causes herself to miscarry` IS FALSE
    `the woman pregnancy is of more than 16 weeks duration as calculated under section 4 of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974` IS FALSE
    `without the consent of the woman` IS TRUE
    `with intent to cause the miscarriage of a woman with child does an act which causes the death of that woman` IS FALSE
    `with intent to destroy the life of a child capable of being born alive` IS FALSE
    `by an intentional act causes a child to die before it has an existence independent of its mother` IS FALSE
    `by such act causes the child to die after its birth` IS FALSE
    `the act was immediately necessary to save the life of the mother` IS FALSE
    `the woman had at a material time been pregnant for a period of 28 weeks or more` IS FALSE
    `does an act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide` IS FALSE
    `by such act causes the death of a quick unborn child` IS FALSE
    `being the father or mother of a child below 12 years of age or having the care of such child` IS FALSE
    `exposes or leaves such child in any place` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of wholly abandoning such child` IS FALSE
    `by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child` IS FALSE
    `intentionally conceals or endeavours to conceal the birth of such child` IS FALSE

-- The same act, within the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974. The 'subject to' opening takes it out of s 312 altogether.
`a lawful termination` MEANS `Unborn And Infants` WITH
    `the act is within the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974` IS TRUE
    `voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry` IS TRUE
    `the woman causes herself to miscarry` IS FALSE
