    `by such act causes the child to die after its birth` IS FALSE
    `the act was immediately necessary to save the life of the mother` IS FALSE
    `the woman had at a material time been pregnant for a period of 28 weeks or more` IS FALSE
    `does an act under such circumstances that if he thereby caused death he would be guilty of culpable homicide` IS FALSE
    `by such act causes the death of a quick unborn child` IS FALSE
    `being the father or mother of a child below 12 years of age or having the care of such child` IS FALSE
    `exposes or leaves such child in any place` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of wholly abandoning such child` IS FALSE
    `by secretly burying or otherwise disposing of the dead body of a child` IS FALSE
    `intentionally conceals or endeavours to conceal the birth of such child` IS FALSE

-- s 315: the act is immediately necessary to save the life of the mother, which the section's own saving takes out.
`a child destroyed to save the mother` MEANS `Unborn And Infants` WITH
    `the act is within the provisions of the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily causes a woman with child to miscarry` IS FALSE
