§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, unborn children and infants`

-- ss 312 and 313.
#ASSERT `constitutes causing miscarriage` `a miscarriage caused without consent`
#ASSERT `constitutes causing miscarriage without consent` `a miscarriage caused without consent`
-- The "subject to the Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974" opening takes the act out.
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes causing miscarriage` `a lawful termination`)
-- s 315 and the saving for the mother's life written into it.
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes child destruction` `a child destroyed to save the mother`)
#ASSERT `constitutes child destruction` `a child destroyed with no such necessity`
-- s 316, on its own Illustration.
#ASSERT `constitutes causing the death of a quick unborn child` `a quick unborn child killed`
-- s 317.
#ASSERT `constitutes exposure and abandonment of a child` `a child abandoned by its mother`

§§ `Assertions -- Chapter 16, kidnapping, abduction, slavery and forced labour`

-- s 361, and its Exception, and the "unless for an immoral or unlawful purpose" that
-- restores the section.
#ASSERT `the person kidnaps from lawful guardianship` `a child taken from its guardian`
#ASSERT `the person kidnaps` `a child taken from its guardian`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person kidnaps from lawful guardianship` `a father taking his own child in good faith`)
#ASSERT `the person kidnaps from lawful guardianship` `a father taking his own child for an unlawful purpose`
-- s 362: abduction is not a kind of kidnapping.
#ASSERT `the person abducts` `an adult deceived into going somewhere`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person kidnaps` `an adult deceived into going somewhere`)
#ASSERT `the person kidnaps or abducts` `an adult deceived into going somewhere`
-- s 364 builds on the abduction.
#ASSERT `constitutes kidnapping or abducting in order to murder` `an abduction in order to murder`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes kidnapping or abducting in order to murder` `an adult deceived into going somewhere`)
-- ss 370, 372 and 374.
#ASSERT `constitutes dealing in a person as a slave` `a person detained as a slave`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes habitual dealing in slaves` `a person detained as a slave`)
#ASSERT `constitutes selling a minor for prostitution` `a minor sold for prostitution`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes buying a minor for prostitution` `a minor sold for prostitution`)
#ASSERT `constitutes unlawful compulsory labour` `a worker compelled to labour`
